"## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design fault-tolerant Unix log ingestion across mixed formats, archives, and rotation, with checkpointing and deduplication.

## Key Concepts

- Log rotation and gz archives
- Mixed log formats (text and JSON)
- Multi-line event parsing
- Event deduplication using fingerprints
- Persistent state and restart safety

## Code Example

```javascript
// Fingerprint function for deduplication
function fingerprint(hour, message) {
  const normalized = (message || '').toLowerCase().trim();
  const hash = require('crypto').createHash('sha256');
  hash.update(`${hour}:${normalized}`);
  return hash.digest('hex');
}

// Checkpoint persistence
function saveCheckpoint(checkpoint) {
  const tempPath = '/tmp/checkpoint.json';
  fs.writeFileSync(tempPath, JSON.stringify(checkpoint));
  fs.renameSync(tempPath, '/path/to/checkpoints.json');
}
```"

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to unify heterogeneous log formats, handle compressed data, and perform time-based validation in a tight, production-like scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-format timestamp extraction (text and JSON)
- Decompression with zcat for .gz files
- Epoch conversion via date -d
- Sliding window filtering (60 minutes) and max absolute skew

## Code Example
```bash
find /logs -type f \( -name '*.log' -o -name '*.log.gz' \) -print0 | while IFS= read -d '' f; do
  case "$f" in
    *.gz) data=$(zcat "$f" 2>/dev/null || echo) ;;
    *) data=$(cat "$f" 2>/dev/null || echo) ;;
  esac
  echo "$data" | awk '
    /^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}/ {
      cmd = "date -d \"" $1 " " $2 "\" +%s 2>/dev/null"
      cmd | getline ts; close(cmd)
      if (ts > 0) print ts
    }
    /{.*"ts".*"lvl".*"msg".*}/ {
      match($0, /"ts":[[:space:]]*[0-9]+/)
      if (RSTART > 0) {
        ts = substr($0, RSTART + 5, RLENGTH - 5)
        print ts
      }
    }
  '
done | awk -v now="$(date +%s)" '
  {
    diff = now - $1
    if (diff <= 3600 && diff >= -3600) {
      abs_diff = (diff < 0) ? -diff : diff
      if (abs_diff > max) max = abs_diff
    }
  }
  END { print max }
'
```
